{"Title":"Proposal for a legislative amendment to the Constitution to cap the state income tax","BillNumber":"S15","DocketNumber":"SD411","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"BET0","Name":"Bruce E. Tarr","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BET0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-14T21:33:31.3"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"BET0","Name":"Bruce E. Tarr","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BET0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-14T21:33:31.3"},{"Id":"PMO","Name":"Patrick M. O'Connor","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/PMO","ResponseDate":"2023-04-06T10:31:12.2533333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S15/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Proposal for Constitutional Amendment","Pinslip":"By Mr. Tarr, a petition (accompanied by proposal, Senate, No. 15) of Bruce E. Tarr for a legislative amendment to the Constitution to cap the state income tax.  Revenue.","DocumentText":"\tArticle 44 of the Massachusetts Constitution is hereby amended by adding the following paragraph at the end thereof:-\r\n\tIn addition to the taxes on income otherwise authorized under this Article, the tax on that portion of annual taxable income shall not be in excess of 6.25 per cent reported on any return related to those taxes. This paragraph shall apply to all tax years beginning on or after January 1, 2023.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Adverse","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J26","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J26"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}